    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d233">

                <pb facs="0318" n="202" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg202"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.51/1211.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-29T15:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 29, 1914, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to your January 27, 8 p.m. Your information about amount of debt is
                    incorrect; $1,200,000 will pay worthy debts now pressing the Government,
                    including salaries. This estimate never included claims of various kinds and
                    Dominican Government asks for additional sum to dispose of the latter. To avoid
                    any mistake I suggest that the amount be left indefinite until ascertained to
                    the satisfaction of Department. Minister for Foreign Affairs expresses the hope
                    that a commercial attaché as suggested by you will be named instead of financial
                    expert.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
